---
description: Read Claude's last reply out loud (neural TTS, with pause/resume)
allowed-tools: Bash(__BIN__:*)
---

Speech output: !`__BIN__ $ARGUMENTS`

The command above already ran during prompt expansion — do NOT run it again.
Report its result to the user in a few words. Say nothing else.

Arguments the user may pass:
- (none)            speak the last reply
- `pause`           suspend playback exactly where it is
- `resume`          continue from the same sample (alias: `unpause`)
- `stop`            abandon playback (alias: `off`)
- `-n 2`            speak the 2nd-most-recent reply
- `follow`          show the text spoken so far, in sync with the audio
- `status`          report whether it is speaking, and the current line
- `engine`          print the current engine
- `engine kokoro`   switch engine persistently (`piper` or `kokoro`)
- `speed`           print the current reading speed
- `speed 1.35`      set the reading speed persistently (0.5-2.0)
- any other text    speak that text verbatim instead
